  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Mapping Frameworks**\n\nI\'m now diving into mapping frameworks. I\'m exploring Leaflet with React-Leaflet, MapLibre GL, and even Cesium. I also see value in 2.5D, Canvas, WebGL, and Leaflet for fast, iframe-friendly rendering without the WebGL context overhead. The goal is ultra-reliable performance.\n\n\n**Exploring Leaflet\'s Capabilities**\n\nI\'m focusing now on Leaflet\'s strengths for our project, especially its speed and reliability. I\'ve confirmed its suitability for 2D, satellite, and hybrid map rendering, with support for various tile layers and data formats. I\'m also impressed by its handling of real-time animation, zero WebGL crash risk, and interactive features. I\'m thinking about a dual view or multi-mode: High-performance 2D Tactical Vector/Satellite Map + Data Radar + Global Telemetry & OSINT Intel streams.\nI\'ve outlined essential packages, including `leaflet`, `@types/leaflet`, `satellite.js`, and potential needs for CORS and confetti, and plan to integrate live data feeds.\n\n\n**Listing Live Data Feeds**\n\nI\'m cataloging live data APIs and feeds, focusing on real-time information. Specifically, I\'ve confirmed several reliable sources: OpenSky Network for live aircraft tracking, CelesTrak for satellites (ISS, Starlink, etc.) using `satellite.js` for precise orbital calculations, and the USGS Earthquake Hazards Program for seismic activity. I\'ll need to expand this list.\n\n\n**Cataloging New Data Sources**\n\nI\'m now expanding my list of live data feeds to include crucial information sources. I\'m focusing on NASA\'s FIRMS and EONET for wildfire and thermal anomaly data. I also see RainViewer API for weather radar, and Open-Meteo for global meteorological telemetry. For maritime tracking, I\'m looking at BarentsWatch AIS, Digitraffic, and others. Lastly, for global intelligence, I\'ll integrate with the GDELT Project 2.0.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Integrations**\n\nI\'m now integrating new, diverse data feeds to broaden the project\'s scope. I\'m focusing on live news with trustworthy sources like Reuters and BBC, ensuring server-side parsing to avoid fabrication. I\'m exploring open infrastructure feeds, including GEM and USGS critical infrastructure data for power grids and energy resources. For financial tracking, I\'m considering Yahoo Finance and CoinGecko for market data. I\'m also looking into public CCTV feeds from Windy, Webcams.travel, and local DOT feeds. Finally, I\'ll adopt the strict data policy.\n\n\n"
