  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Geospatial Schemas**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing a clean architecture, starting with `src/types.ts`. I\'m defining core geospatial schemas here, including live object models, provider metadata like source and status, various layers and filters, and coordinate structures. The goal is to establish a canonical foundation for our spatial data processing.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Fetching**\n\nNow, I\'m working on the data fetching and API proxying logic within `server.ts`. It\'s an Express backend with server-side caching and rate-limiting to handle open data APIs like OpenSky and CelesTrak. I\'m focusing on strict error reporting and delivering accurate data, even under rate limits, without fabricating responses. I\'m structuring endpoints for audit, flight tracking, satellites, earthquakes, wildfires, and weather.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Sources**\n\nI\'ve been broadening the data sources. Specifically, I\'m integrating RainViewer radar data with Open-Meteo atmospheric metrics. I\'m also adding `/api/infrastructure` for open energy infrastructure, `/api/news` for real-time alerts, and `/api/macro` for commodity benchmarks. I\'m building `/api/sources/health` to monitor provider health. The `/api/gemini/briefing` endpoint will provide situational intelligence summaries. Finally, I\'ve started building the `TacticalMap.tsx` component.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the front-end interactive components, specifically the tactical map and its supporting UI. I\'m working on overlays using custom SVG icons, including aircraft with heading rotation, ground tracks for satellites, earthquake rings, fire hotspots, radar frames, and infrastructure markers. I\'m also implementing a click-to-inspect detail drawer and viewport bounding box filtering, and range measurement tools.\n\nI\'m developing the UI components to give relevant status and controls, with: a system clock, threat level display, a feed status ticker, source health indicators, an audit drawer toggle, an AI briefing trigger, and layer toggle presets, all within `Header.tsx`. I\'m also building a collapsible hierarchical layer control panel, showing the current data, freshness indicators, opacity controls and filter filters, in `LayerControlPanel.tsx`. Finally, in `IntelFeedPanel.tsx`, I\'m developing a real-time chronological telemetry event stream, with events and map integration. In `ObjectDetailDrawer.tsx` I\'m making a data policy inspector, showing the raw identifier, provider and source, and their source URLs.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_622961"
      name: "create_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Content\":\"export type SourceStatus = \'VERIFIED LIVE\' | \'REQUIRES KEY\' | \'BROKEN\' | \'STATIC DATA\' | \'MOCK/DEMO\' | \'UNKNOWN\' | \'SOURCE UNAVAILABLE\';\\n\\nexport interface DataProvenance {\\n  provider: string;\\n  sourceUrl: string;\\n  adapter: string;\\n  fetched_at: string;\\n  freshness_seconds?: number;\\n  status: SourceStatus;\\n  raw_identifier?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface AircraftRecord extends DataProvenance {\\n  icao24: string;\\n  callsign: string;\\n  origin_country: string;\\n  time_position: number;\\n  last_contact: number;\\n  longitude: number;\\n  latitude: number;\\n  baro_altitude: number | null; // meters\\n  on_ground: boolean;\\n  velocity: number | null; // m/s\\n  true_track: number | null; // degrees 0-360\\n  vertical_rate: number | null; // m/s\\n  geo_altitude: number | null;\\n  squawk: string | null;\\n  spi: boolean;\\n  position_source: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface SatelliteRecord extends DataProvenance {\\n  noradId: string;\\n  name: string;\\n  line1: string;\\n  line2: string;\\n  group: \'stations\' | \'starlink\' | \'weather\' | \'active\';\\n  calculated?: {\\n    latitude: number;\\n    longitude: number;\\n    altitudeKm: number;\\n    velocityKmS: number;\\n    footprintRadiusKm: number;\\n    periodMinutes: number;\\n    inclinationDeg: number;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport interface EarthquakeRecord extends DataProvenance {\\n  id: string;\\n  magnitude: number;\\n  place: string;\\n  time: number;\\n  updated: number;\\n  tz: number | null;\\n  url: string;\\n  detail: string;\\n  felt: number | null;\\n  cdi: number | null;\\n  mmi: number | null;\\n  alert: string | null;\\n  status: string;\\n  tsunami: number;\\n  sig: number;\\n  net: string;\\n  code: string;\\n  ids: string;\\n  sources: string;\\n  types: string;\\n  nst: number | null;\\n  dmin: number | null;\\n  rms: number | null;\\n  gap: number | null;\\n  magType: string;\\n  type: string;\\n  title: string;\\