  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "This summary captures the current state of the GOD-VIEW-LAB project, an ongoing effort to build a unified geospatial intelligence platform.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **Build the full end product:** The user requested a \"whole end product\" that integrates all identified data sources effectively, ensuring all dependencies are handled and the system is error-free. (Status: IMPLEMENTATION)\n*   **Strict Data Policy Compliance:** The user mandated \"NO FAKE DATA.\" All visualizations must be based on live telemetry, with explicit handling for failed sources (\"SOURCE UNAVAILABLE\"). (Status: IMPLEMENTATION)\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n*   **Core Directive:** \"NO FAKE DATA.\" Never invent API endpoints or fabricate observations.\n*   **Data Integrity Rule:** \"A failed source must display SOURCE UNAVAILABLE.\"\n*   **Provenance Requirement:** Every live object must retain: `source/provider`, `source URL or adapter`, `fetched_at timestamp`, `freshness/status`, and `raw identifier`.\n*   **Repositories Provided for Audit:**\n    1. `bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view` (Canonical)\n    2. `deco31416/worldmonitor`\n    3. `hendrikbgr/open-live-map`\n    4. `NoahSBrown/Argus`\n    5. `Sudhendra/gigawattmap`\n    6. `girubato/active_fire_dashboard`\n    7. `TerriaJS/terriajs`\n    8. `TerriaJS/TerriaMap`\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **Repository Audit:** Completed a comprehensive audit of all 8 repositories, identifying key strengths (e.g., `gods-eye-view` for 3D globe, `worldmonitor` for OSINT, `gigawattmap` for infrastructure) and risks (e.g., CORS issues, licensing, mock data fallbacks).\n*   **Architecture Design:** Established a Node.js/Express backend proxy architecture to handle CORS, rate limiting, and data sanitization, serving a React/Leaflet frontend.\n*   **Backend Implementation:** Created `server.ts` which implements secure proxies for:\n    *   OpenSky Network (Flights)\n    *   CelesTrak (Satellites)\n    *   USGS (Earthquakes)\n    *   NASA EONET (Wildfires/Hazards)\n    *   RainViewer (Weather Radar)\n    *   GDELT (News/Geopolitics)\n    *   Static Infrastructure Registry (Nuclear/Datacenters/Cables)\n    *   Macroeconomic Radar (CoinGecko/EIA)\n*   **Frontend Components:** Created modular UI components:\n    *   `Header.tsx`: Tactical dashboard controls.\n    *   `LayerControlPanel.tsx`: Layer toggles and filtering.\n    *   `ObjectDetailDrawer.tsx`: Detailed data inspection and provenance display.\n    *   `TacticalMap.tsx`: Leaflet-based map engine with support for custom SVG markers and layer groups.\n*   **Utilities:** Created `src/services/satellitePropagator.ts` using `satellite.js` to calculate real-time orbital positions from TLE data.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture:** The backend (`server.ts`) is the single source of truth for data. It implements an in-memory cache with configurable TTLs to respect external API rate limits.\n*   **Data Flow:** Frontend components fetch from `/api/*` endpoints. The backend handles authentication (e.g., `OPENSKY_USERNAME`, `NASA_FIRMS_MAP_KEY`) and CORS.\n*   **Failures/Constraints:**\n    *   Direct client-side fetching from external APIs (like OpenSky) fails due to CORS. The backend proxy is mandatory.\n    *   `satellite.js` is used for client-side orbital propagation, but the TLE data is fetched via the server.\n    *   The `active_fire_dashboard` repo contained a \"mock data fallback.\" This was explicitly **removed** in the implementation to comply with the \"NO FAKE DATA\" policy.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited/Created Files:**\n    *   `/metadata.json`: Updated project metadata.\n    *   `/package.json`: Added `leaflet`, `satellite.js`, and build scripts.\n    *   `/index.html`: Injected Leaflet CSS and custom fonts.\n    *   `/.env.example`: Added placeholders for API keys.\n    *   `/src/types.ts`: Defined strict TypeScript interfaces for all data domains.\n    *   `/src/services/satellitePropagator.ts`: Created orbital math utility.\n    *   `/server.ts`: Created the full-stack proxy server.\n    *   `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Created.\n    *   `/src/components/LayerControlPanel.tsx`: Created.\n    *   `/src/components/ObjectDetailDrawer.tsx`: Created.\n    *   `/src/components/TacticalMap.tsx`: Created.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Immediate Status:** The infrastructure (backend and components) is built, but the components are not yet connected to the data flow in `App.tsx`.\n*   **Next Steps:**\n    1.  **Integrate `App.tsx`:** Update `src/App.tsx` to fetch data from the `/api/*` endpoints defined in `server.ts` (e.g., `fetch(\'/api/flights\')`).\n    2.  **State Management:** Manage the global state for layers, selected objects, and fetched data within `App.tsx`.\n    3.  **Connect Components:** Pass the fetched data and state handlers into `TacticalMap`, `LayerControlPanel`, and `Header`.\n    4.  **Verification:** Verify that the map renders the live telemetry and that the \"ObjectDetailDrawer\" displays the correct provenance metadata.\n*   **Reference:** The next agent should start by reading `src/App.tsx` to understand where to hook in the data fetching logic."
    included_step_index_end: 42
    conversation_log_uris: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/b302fb21-27d7-41f3-b06d-17b4dcccddc4/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl"
    user_requests: "User prompt: You are working in an isolated GOD-VIEW-LAB.\n\nThe attached/imported repositories are REFERENCE IMPLEMENTATIONS. Do NOT modify ASTRA, FMB or TECHNICALS and do NOT blindly merge these repositories.\n\nCRITICAL RULE:\nNO FAKE DATA.\n\nBefore writing or changing application code, audit every supplied repository.\n\nFor every repository identify:\n\n1. Repository name and source.\n2. License.\n3. Framework/stack.\n4. Map/rendering engine.\n5. Every external data source/API/feed.\n6. Exact file/module implementing each data adapter.\n7. Whether each source currently appears:\n\n   * VERIFIED LIVE\n   * REQUIRES KEY\n   * BROKEN\n   * STATIC DATA\n   * MOCK/DEMO\n   * UNKNOWN\n8. Authentication requirements.\n9. CORS/server-proxy requirements.\n10. Rate limits if documented.\n11. Duplicate capabilities across repositories.\n12. Which implementation is technically strongest for each capability.\n\nSTRICT DATA POLICY:\n\n* Never invent API endpoints.\n* Never fabricate coordinates, events, aircraft, vessels, cameras, infrastructure, prices, news or other live observations.\n* Never replace a failed API with generated/sample/demo data unless explicitly placed in a clearly labelled DEMO mode.\n* No hidden fallback to mock JSON.\n* A failed source must display SOURCE UNAVAILABLE.\n* UNKNOWN must never become VERIFIED.\n* Every live object eventually shown in the application must retain:\n  source/provider\n  source URL or adapter\n  fetched_at timestamp\n  freshness/status\n  raw identifier when available.\n\nDo not build the final application yet.\n\nOUTPUT FIRST:\n\nA. Repository audit\nB. Data-source registry\nC. Feature-overlap matrix\nD. Licensing risks\nE. Working vs broken sources\nF. Recommended canonical implementation for each layer\nG. Proposed GOD-VIEW-LAB architecture\nH. Exact capabilities that can genuinely operate in the AI Studio environment\n\nSTOP after the audit and wait for the next instruction.\n\nhow do I send the zip files or links ??God\342\200\231s Eye View \342\200\224 core 3D globe + aircraft/ships/satellites/cameras\nGitHub \342\200\224 bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view\nThis is the canonical repo and is currently on v0.1.1.\nWorldMonitor \342\200\224 global news + geopolitical + finance + infrastructure intelligence\nGitHub \342\200\224 WorldMonitor\nIt includes 3D/2D mapping, 45 data layers, finance radar, infrastructure and news aggregation.\nOpen Live Map \342\200\224 cleaner live-map implementation/reference\nGitHub \342\200\224 hendrikbgr/open-live-map\nGigawatt Map \342\200\224 power plants/data centres/infrastructure, particularly useful for ASTRA\nGitHub \342\200\224 Sudhendra/gigawattmap\nActive Fire Dashboard \342\200\224 NASA FIRMS wildfire/event layer\nGitHub \342\200\224 girubato/active_fire_dashboard\nOne warning: this repo currently contains a sample-data fallback when the backend fails, so AI Studio must explicitly remove/disable that behavior for production.\nTerriaJS \342\200\224 serious geospatial platform architecture for large numbers of layers\nGitHub \342\200\224 TerriaJS/terriajs\nIt supports Cesium 3D, 2D fallback and very large layer catalogs.\nDownload\nFor each page:\nCode \342\206\222 Download ZIP\nThen you\'ll have roughly:\ngods-eye-view-main.zip\nworldmonitor-main.zip\nopen-live-map-main.zip\ngigawattmap-main.zip\nactive_fire_dashboard-main.zip\nterriajs-main.zip\nThose are the six I would upload \n\n\n1. bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view\n2. deco31416/worldmonitor\n3. hendrikbgr/open-live-map\n4. NoahSBrown/Argus\n5. Sudhendra/gigawattmap\n6. girubato/active_fire_dashboard\n7. TerriaJS/terriajs\n8. TerriaJS/TerriaMap\n\nfull free hand no erros please get it sorted and ensure all dependencies are done if needed use free hand give me a whole end product \nso include all your suggestions already and make it work for a unified geospatial visualization platform that integrates all these data sources effectively.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
