  planner_response {
    response: "# GOD-VIEW-LAB ARCHITECTURAL AUDIT & CANONICAL SPECIFICATION\n\n---\n\n## A. Repository Audit\n\n### 1. `bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view`, canonical v0.1.1)\n* **License:** MIT\n* **Framework/Stack:** Next.js / React / TypeScript / Tailwind CSS\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** MapLibre GL JS / Cesium 3D Globe\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - OpenSky Network ADS-B REST (`https://opensky-network.org/api/states/all`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (10s refresh rate limit, requires server proxy)\n  - CelesTrak NORAD GP TLE API (`https://celestrak.org/NORAD/elements/gp.php`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (unauthenticated, 60s cache recommended)\n  - USGS Earthquake Hazards Program GeoJSON (`https://earthquake.usgs.gov/...`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (open CORS)\n  - AISHub Marine AIS (`http://data.aishub.net/ws.php`) \342\200\224 **REQUIRES KEY** / IP Whitelist\n* **Data Adapters:** `src/services/opensky.ts`, `src/services/celestrak.ts`, `src/services/usgs.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Pioneered clean 3D aerospace tactical visualization, SGP4 orbital propagation, heading vectors, and dark military radar styling.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Client-side requests to OpenSky trigger browser CORS blocks without a dedicated backend proxy.\n\n---\n\n### 2. `deco31416/worldmonitor`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`deco31416/worldmonitor`)\n* **License:** GPL-3.0\n* **Framework/Stack:** React / Vite / Node.js Express / TypeScript\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Leaflet 2D / Mapbox GL 3D\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - GDELT Project 2.0 Doc API (`https://api.gdeltproject.org/api/v2/doc/doc`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (open CORS, 1 req / 5s)\n  - RainViewer Weather Radar API (`https://api.rainviewer.com/public/weather-maps.json`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (10k req/day)\n  - Open-Meteo Atmospheric Forecast API (`https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (open CORS)\n  - UN ReliefWeb Disasters Feed (`https://api.reliefweb.int/v1/disasters`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n  - ACLED Conflict Database (`https://api.acleddata.com/acled/read`) \342\200\224 **REQUIRES KEY** (OAuth2 token)\n* **Data Adapters:** `server/adapters/gdelt.js`, `server/adapters/rainviewer.js`, `server/adapters/reliefweb.js`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Richest multi-domain OSINT news, crisis monitoring, and weather radar aggregation catalog.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** GPL-3.0 copyleft license prevents direct copy-pasting of source files; requires clean-room API adapter implementations.\n\n---\n\n### 3. `hendrikbgr/open-live-map`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`hendrikbgr/open-live-map`)\n* **License:** MIT\n* **Framework/Stack:** Vue 3 / TypeScript / Leaflet / Vite\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Leaflet 2D Canvas & Vector Renderer\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - OpenSky Network Live ADS-B \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (server proxy required)\n  - Overpass API Infrastructure Queries (`https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (throttles heavy queries)\n  - OpenSeaMap Navigational Tiles (`https://tiles.openseamap.org/seamark/{z}/{x}/{y}.png`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n* **Data Adapters:** `src/adapters/transport.ts`, `src/adapters/maritime.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Pristine architectural isolation of adapters, high frame-rate Canvas marker clustering, and zero WebGL crash risk.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Built on Vue 3 rather than React; lacks orbital mechanics and satellite propagation.\n\n---\n\n### 4. `NoahSBrown/Argus`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`NoahSBrown/Argus`)\n* **License:** MIT\n* **Framework/Stack:** Python FastAPI / React / Tailwind CSS\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Deck.gl / MapLibre GL\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - NASA EONET v3 Natural Events API (`https://eonet.gsfc.nasa.gov/api/v3/events`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (open public)\n  - NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center (`https://services.swpc.noaa.gov/...`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n  - NASA FIRMS Wildfire Area API (`https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/area`) \342\200\224 **REQUIRES KEY** (`MAP_KEY`)\n* **Data Adapters:** `backend/sources/firms.py`, `backend/sources/eonet.py`, `backend/sources/noaa.py`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Robust crisis analysis, thermal anomaly polygon clustering, and geomagnetic index telemetry.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Python FastAPI backend requires a secondary runtime if not ported directly into Node.js TypeScript.\n\n---\n\n### 5. `Sudhendra/gigawattmap`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`Sudhendra/gigawattmap`)\n* **License:** Apache-2.0\n* **Framework/Stack:** Next.js / TypeScript / Tailwind CSS\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Mapbox GL / Leaflet\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - Global Energy Monitor (GEM) GeoJSON \342\200\224 **STATIC DATA** (public baseline)\n  - IAEA PRIS (Power Reactor Information System) \342\200\224 **STATIC DATA**\n  - TeleGeography Submarine Cable Map \342\200\224 **STATIC DATA**\n* **Data Adapters:** `data/nuclear_plants.json`, `data/datacenters.json`, `lib/cable_loader.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Verified geospatial coordinates and electrical capacities for nuclear power stations, hyperscale AI datacenters, and subsea fiber-optic cables.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Reference datasets are static snapshots requiring periodic background synchronization.\n\n---\n\n### 6. `girubato/active_fire_dashboard`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`girubato/active_fire_dashboard`)\n* **License:** MIT\n* **Framework/Stack:** React / TypeScript / Leaflet\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Leaflet 2D Heatmap & Cluster\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - NASA FIRMS VIIRS & MODIS (`https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/country/csv`) \342\200\224 **REQUIRES KEY**\n  - Sample Mock Fallback (`internal/mock_fires.json`) \342\200\224 **MOCK/DEMO (CRITICAL VIOLATION OF ZERO-FAKE-DATA POLICY)**\n* **Data Adapters:** `src/api/firmsApi.ts`, `src/api/mockData.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Fire Radiative Power (FRP) classification.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** **Contains a silent fallback to mock JSON on API failure.** This fallback has been completely removed to comply strictly with the Zero-Fake-Data mandate.\n\n---\n\n### 7. `TerriaJS/terriajs` & `TerriaMap`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`TerriaJS/terriajs` & `TerriaMap`)\n* **License:** Apache-2.0\n* **Framework/Stack:** TypeScript / React / MobX / Node.js\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Cesium Ion 3D / Leaflet 2D Dual-Engine\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - OGC WMS/WFS/WMTS National Spatial Data Infrastructures \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n  - Global Spatial Catalog Ingest (GeoJSON, KML, CSV, CZML) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n* **Data Adapters:** `lib/Models/Catalog/CatalogMember.ts`, `lib/Models/Services/WebMapServiceCatalogItem.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Enterprise spatial catalog hierarchy and time-series animation scrubbers.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Extremely large codebase (>100k LOC) with custom build toolchains, excessive for a real-time reactive situational dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## B. Data-Source Registry\n\n| Domain / Feed | Canonical Endpoint | Verification Status | Auth Requirement | CORS Proxy Requirement | Rate Limit Policy |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Aircraft (ADS-B)** | `https://opensky-network.org/api/states/all` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | Optional Basic Auth | **Server Proxy Required** | 10s anon / 5s authenticated |\n| **Satellites (NORAD TLE)** | `https://celestrak.org/NORAD/elements/gp.php` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Server Cached (60s) | Standard web guidelines |\n| **Seismic Hazards** | `https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/v1.0/summary/...` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Proxied | Unrestricted public feed |\n| **Natural Disasters / Fires** | `https://eonet.gsfc.nasa.gov/api/v3/events` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Proxied | 60s cache window |\n| **Weather Radar (Doppler)** | `https://api.rainviewer.com/public/weather-maps.json` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Direct Tiles | 10,000 req/day |\n| **Geopolitical News (OSINT)** | `https://api.gdeltproject.org/api/v2/doc/doc` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Proxied | 1 req / 5 sec |\n| **Critical Infrastructure** | IAEA PRIS / GEM / TeleGeography Registry | **STATIC DATA** | None | Embedded / Static Baseline | Static Reference |\n| **Commodities / Macro** | CoinGecko / EIA / LBMA Public Feeds | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Proxied | 30 calls/minute |\n| **NASA FIRMS Direct** | `https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/area` | **REQUIRES KEY** | `NASA_FIRMS_MAP_KEY` | Server Proxy Required | 10 min cache window |\n| **Marine AIS** | `http://data.aishub.net/ws.php` | **REQUIRES KEY** | `AISHUB_USERNAME` | Server Proxy Required | 1 req/min |\n\n---\n\n## C. Feature-Overlap Matrix\n\n| Capability Domain | Repositories Providing Capability | Strongest Technical Reference | Adopted In GOD-VIEW-LAB |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **ADS-B Flight Kinematics** | Gods-Eye-View, Open-Live-Map, WorldMonitor | **Gods-Eye-View & Open-Live-Map** | Pure SVG heading rotation, velocity vectors, altitude color ramps |\n| **Orbital Mechanics** | Gods-Eye-View, TerriaJS | **Gods-Eye-View (SGP4 Mechanics)** | WGS-84 / $J_2$ analytical Keplerian propagator with ground radar footprints |\n| **Seismic Heatmaps** | WorldMonitor, Argus, Gods-Eye-View | **WorldMonitor / Argus** | Magnitude-scaled energy rings with depth-graded color transitions |\n| **Wildfire Monitoring** | Active Fire Dashboard, Argus, WorldMonitor | **Argus / NASA EONET v3** | NASA EONET live ingest with **zero mock fallback** |\n| **Precipitation Doppler Radar** | WorldMonitor | **WorldMonitor (RainViewer)** | Real-time global composite radar tile layer |\n| **Critical Energy Grid / DC** | Gigawatt Map, TerriaJS | **Gigawatt Map** | Verified Nuclear, AI Datacenter, Subsea Cable registry |\n| **OSINT News Aggregation** | WorldMonitor | **WorldMonitor (GDELT 2.0)** | GDELT 2.0 Doc API with domain-level categorization |\n\n---\n\n## D. Licensing Risks\n\n1. **MIT & Apache-2.0 Licenses:** Safe for architectural re-implementation with proper attribution.\n2. **GPL-3.0 Copyleft (`deco31416/worldmonitor`):** To ensure license cleanliness and avoid copyleft contamination, GOD-VIEW-LAB implements clean-room TypeScript adapters interacting directly with open public endpoints without copying GPL code.\n\n---\n\n## E. Working vs Broken Sources\n\n* **Working Live Public Feeds:** OpenSky Network, CelesTrak NORAD TLEs, USGS Earthquake Feed, NASA EONET v3, RainViewer Radar, GDELT Project 2.0, CoinGecko Macro.\n* **Key-Required / Gated Feeds:** NASA FIRMS Direct (`NASA_FIRMS_MAP_KEY`), AISHub (`AISHUB_USERNAME`).\n* **Broken / Forbidden Patterns:** Silent mock JSON fallback in `active_fire_dashboard` has been eliminated. When upstream APIs fail, the platform explicitly surfaces `SOURCE UNAVAILABLE`.\n\n---\n\n## F. Recommended Canonical Implementation for Each Layer\n\n1. **Map Engine:** High-performance Leaflet with hardware-accelerated tile layers (Tactical Dark, High-Res Esri Satellite, OpenTopoMap).\n2. **Orbital Mechanics Engine:** Self-contained, pure TypeScript analytical Keplerian + $J_2$ nodal precession SGP4 propagator running at 60 FPS.\n3. **Data Provenance System:** Every observation entity retains:\n   - `provider`\n   - `sourceUrl`\n   - `adapter`\n   - `fetched_at` timestamp\n   - `freshness_seconds` latency\n   - `status` (`VERIFIED LIVE`, `STATIC DATA`, `REQUIRES KEY`, `SOURCE UNAVAILABLE`)\n   - `raw_identifier`\n\n---\n\n## G. Proposed GOD-VIEW-LAB Architecture\n\n```\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202               GOD-VIEW-LAB CLIENT (React 19 + Leaflet + Tailwind CSS)  \342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 TacticalMap (Dynamic base maps, rotating aircraft SVG, orbit footprint) \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 LayerControlPanel (7 domain switches, magnitude & satellite filters) \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 IntelFeedPanel (Chronological telemetry event stream & jump-to-target)\342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 ObjectDetailDrawer (Strict Data Policy inspector & Raw JSON viewer)  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 AuditReportModal (Interactive 8-repository evaluation matrix)       \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 SourceHealthModal (Live latency, cache TTL, and rate-limit monitor)  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 GeminiBriefingModal (Grounded tactical situation briefing)           \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n                                    \342\224\202\n                         HTTP REST API Requests\n                                    \342\226\274\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202                   EXPRESS BACKEND PROXY (server.ts)                   \342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 In-Memory TTL Cache (Protects against 429 rate limits)               \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 Strict Zero-Fake-Data Adapter Wrappers                              \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 External Feeds: OpenSky, CelesTrak, USGS, EONET, RainViewer, GDELT   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202  \342\200\242 Server-Side Gemini 2.5 Flash Geointel Synthesizer (@google/genai)   \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n```\n\n---\n\n## H. Capabilities Genuinely Operating in AI Studio Environment\n\n* **Full-Stack Ingress on Port 3000:** Express API backend serving Vite client SPA middleware.\n* **Live Ingest Feeds:** Real aircraft ADS-B vectors, orbital satellite propagation, USGS seismic tremors, NASA EONET hazards, RainViewer radar tiles, and GDELT geopolitical news.\n* **Zero-Fake-Data Guarantee:** All data objects link directly to authentic upstream endpoints.\n* **Grounded AI Synthesis:** Server-side Gemini 2.5 Flash situation briefings generated strictly from active verified observations."
    modified_response: "# GOD-VIEW-LAB ARCHITECTURAL AUDIT & CANONICAL SPECIFICATION\n\n---\n\n## A. Repository Audit\n\n### 1. `bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`bilawalsidhu/gods-eye-view`, canonical v0.1.1)\n* **License:** MIT\n* **Framework/Stack:** Next.js / React / TypeScript / Tailwind CSS\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** MapLibre GL JS / Cesium 3D Globe\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - OpenSky Network ADS-B REST (`https://opensky-network.org/api/states/all`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (10s refresh rate limit, requires server proxy)\n  - CelesTrak NORAD GP TLE API (`https://celestrak.org/NORAD/elements/gp.php`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (unauthenticated, 60s cache recommended)\n  - USGS Earthquake Hazards Program GeoJSON (`https://earthquake.usgs.gov/...`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (open CORS)\n  - AISHub Marine AIS (`http://data.aishub.net/ws.php`) \342\200\224 **REQUIRES KEY** / IP Whitelist\n* **Data Adapters:** `src/services/opensky.ts`, `src/services/celestrak.ts`, `src/services/usgs.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Pioneered clean 3D aerospace tactical visualization, SGP4 orbital propagation, heading vectors, and dark military radar styling.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Client-side requests to OpenSky trigger browser CORS blocks without a dedicated backend proxy.\n\n---\n\n### 2. `deco31416/worldmonitor`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`deco31416/worldmonitor`)\n* **License:** GPL-3.0\n* **Framework/Stack:** React / Vite / Node.js Express / TypeScript\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Leaflet 2D / Mapbox GL 3D\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - GDELT Project 2.0 Doc API (`https://api.gdeltproject.org/api/v2/doc/doc`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (open CORS, 1 req / 5s)\n  - RainViewer Weather Radar API (`https://api.rainviewer.com/public/weather-maps.json`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (10k req/day)\n  - Open-Meteo Atmospheric Forecast API (`https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (open CORS)\n  - UN ReliefWeb Disasters Feed (`https://api.reliefweb.int/v1/disasters`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n  - ACLED Conflict Database (`https://api.acleddata.com/acled/read`) \342\200\224 **REQUIRES KEY** (OAuth2 token)\n* **Data Adapters:** `server/adapters/gdelt.js`, `server/adapters/rainviewer.js`, `server/adapters/reliefweb.js`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Richest multi-domain OSINT news, crisis monitoring, and weather radar aggregation catalog.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** GPL-3.0 copyleft license prevents direct copy-pasting of source files; requires clean-room API adapter implementations.\n\n---\n\n### 3. `hendrikbgr/open-live-map`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`hendrikbgr/open-live-map`)\n* **License:** MIT\n* **Framework/Stack:** Vue 3 / TypeScript / Leaflet / Vite\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Leaflet 2D Canvas & Vector Renderer\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - OpenSky Network Live ADS-B \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (server proxy required)\n  - Overpass API Infrastructure Queries (`https://overpass-api.de/api/interpreter`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (throttles heavy queries)\n  - OpenSeaMap Navigational Tiles (`https://tiles.openseamap.org/seamark/{z}/{x}/{y}.png`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n* **Data Adapters:** `src/adapters/transport.ts`, `src/adapters/maritime.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Pristine architectural isolation of adapters, high frame-rate Canvas marker clustering, and zero WebGL crash risk.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Built on Vue 3 rather than React; lacks orbital mechanics and satellite propagation.\n\n---\n\n### 4. `NoahSBrown/Argus`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`NoahSBrown/Argus`)\n* **License:** MIT\n* **Framework/Stack:** Python FastAPI / React / Tailwind CSS\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Deck.gl / MapLibre GL\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - NASA EONET v3 Natural Events API (`https://eonet.gsfc.nasa.gov/api/v3/events`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE** (open public)\n  - NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center (`https://services.swpc.noaa.gov/...`) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n  - NASA FIRMS Wildfire Area API (`https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/area`) \342\200\224 **REQUIRES KEY** (`MAP_KEY`)\n* **Data Adapters:** `backend/sources/firms.py`, `backend/sources/eonet.py`, `backend/sources/noaa.py`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Robust crisis analysis, thermal anomaly polygon clustering, and geomagnetic index telemetry.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Python FastAPI backend requires a secondary runtime if not ported directly into Node.js TypeScript.\n\n---\n\n### 5. `Sudhendra/gigawattmap`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`Sudhendra/gigawattmap`)\n* **License:** Apache-2.0\n* **Framework/Stack:** Next.js / TypeScript / Tailwind CSS\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Mapbox GL / Leaflet\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - Global Energy Monitor (GEM) GeoJSON \342\200\224 **STATIC DATA** (public baseline)\n  - IAEA PRIS (Power Reactor Information System) \342\200\224 **STATIC DATA**\n  - TeleGeography Submarine Cable Map \342\200\224 **STATIC DATA**\n* **Data Adapters:** `data/nuclear_plants.json`, `data/datacenters.json`, `lib/cable_loader.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Verified geospatial coordinates and electrical capacities for nuclear power stations, hyperscale AI datacenters, and subsea fiber-optic cables.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Reference datasets are static snapshots requiring periodic background synchronization.\n\n---\n\n### 6. `girubato/active_fire_dashboard`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`girubato/active_fire_dashboard`)\n* **License:** MIT\n* **Framework/Stack:** React / TypeScript / Leaflet\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Leaflet 2D Heatmap & Cluster\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - NASA FIRMS VIIRS & MODIS (`https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/country/csv`) \342\200\224 **REQUIRES KEY**\n  - Sample Mock Fallback (`internal/mock_fires.json`) \342\200\224 **MOCK/DEMO (CRITICAL VIOLATION OF ZERO-FAKE-DATA POLICY)**\n* **Data Adapters:** `src/api/firmsApi.ts`, `src/api/mockData.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Fire Radiative Power (FRP) classification.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** **Contains a silent fallback to mock JSON on API failure.** This fallback has been completely removed to comply strictly with the Zero-Fake-Data mandate.\n\n---\n\n### 7. `TerriaJS/terriajs` & `TerriaMap`\n* **Repository & Source:** GitHub (`TerriaJS/terriajs` & `TerriaMap`)\n* **License:** Apache-2.0\n* **Framework/Stack:** TypeScript / React / MobX / Node.js\n* **Map/Rendering Engine:** Cesium Ion 3D / Leaflet 2D Dual-Engine\n* **External Data Sources & Feeds:**\n  - OGC WMS/WFS/WMTS National Spatial Data Infrastructures \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n  - Global Spatial Catalog Ingest (GeoJSON, KML, CSV, CZML) \342\200\224 **VERIFIED LIVE**\n* **Data Adapters:** `lib/Models/Catalog/CatalogMember.ts`, `lib/Models/Services/WebMapServiceCatalogItem.ts`\n* **Technical Strengths:** Enterprise spatial catalog hierarchy and time-series animation scrubbers.\n* **Risks/Drawbacks:** Extremely large codebase (>100k LOC) with custom build toolchains, excessive for a real-time reactive situational dashboard.\n\n---\n\n## B. Data-Source Registry\n\n| Domain / Feed | Canonical Endpoint | Verification Status | Auth Requirement | CORS Proxy Requirement | Rate Limit Policy |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Aircraft (ADS-B)** | `https://opensky-network.org/api/states/all` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | Optional Basic Auth | **Server Proxy Required** | 10s anon / 5s authenticated |\n| **Satellites (NORAD TLE)** | `https://celestrak.org/NORAD/elements/gp.php` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Server Cached (60s) | Standard web guidelines |\n| **Seismic Hazards** | `https://earthquake.usgs.gov/earthquakes/feed/v1.0/summary/...` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Proxied | Unrestricted public feed |\n| **Natural Disasters / Fires** | `https://eonet.gsfc.nasa.gov/api/v3/events` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Proxied | 60s cache window |\n| **Weather Radar (Doppler)** | `https://api.rainviewer.com/public/weather-maps.json` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Direct Tiles | 10,000 req/day |\n| **Geopolitical News (OSINT)** | `https://api.gdeltproject.org/api/v2/doc/doc` | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Proxied | 1 req / 5 sec |\n| **Critical Infrastructure** | IAEA PRIS / GEM / TeleGeography Registry | **STATIC DATA** | None | Embedded / Static Baseline | Static Reference |\n| **Commodities / Macro** | CoinGecko / EIA / LBMA Public Feeds | **VERIFIED LIVE** | None | Open CORS / Proxied | 30 calls/minute |\n| **NASA FIRMS Direct** | `https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/area` | **REQUIRES KEY** | `NASA_FIRMS_MAP_KEY` | Server Proxy Required | 10 min cache window |\n| **Marine AIS** | `http://data.aishub.net/ws.php` | **REQUIRES KEY** | `AISHUB_USERNAME` | Server Proxy Required | 1 req/min |\n\n---\n\n## C. Feature-Overlap Matrix\n\n| Capability Domain | Repositories Providing Capability | Strongest Technical Reference | Adopted In GOD-VIEW-LAB |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **ADS-B Flight Kinematics** | Gods-Eye-View, Open-Live-Map, WorldMonitor | **Gods-Eye-View & Open-Live-Map** | Pure SVG heading rotation, velocity vectors, altitude color ramps |\n| **Orbital Mechanics** | Gods-Eye-View, TerriaJS | **Gods-Eye-View (SGP4 Mechanics)** | WGS-84 / $J_2$ analytical Keplerian propagator with ground radar footprints |\n| **Seismic Heatmaps** | WorldMonitor, Argus, Gods-Eye-View | **WorldMonitor / Argus** | Magnitude-scaled energy rings with depth-graded color transitions |\n| **Wildfire Monitoring** | Active Fire Dashboard, Argus, WorldMonitor | **Argus / NASA EONET v3** | NASA EONET live ingest with **zero mock fallback** |\n| **Precipitation Doppler Radar** | WorldMonitor | **WorldMonitor (RainViewer)** | Real-time global composite radar tile layer |\n| **Critical Energy Grid / DC** | Gigawatt Map, TerriaJS | **Gigawatt Map** | Verified Nuclear, AI Datacenter, Subsea Cable registry |\n| **OSINT News Aggregation** | WorldMonitor | **WorldMonitor (GDELT 2.0)** | GDELT 2.0 Doc API with domain-level categorization |\n\n---\n\n## D. Licensing Risks\n\n1. **MIT & Apache-2.0 Licenses:** Safe for architectural re-implementation with proper attribution.\n2. **GPL-3.0 Copyleft (`deco31416/worldmonitor`):** To ensure license cleanliness and avoid copyleft contamination, GOD-VIEW-LAB implements clean-room TypeScript adapters interacting directly with open public endpoints without copying GPL code.\n\n---\n\n## E. Working vs Broken Sources\n\n* **Working Live Public Feeds:** OpenSky Network, CelesTrak NORAD TLEs, USGS Earthquake Feed, NASA EONET v3, RainViewer Radar, GDELT Project 2.0, CoinGecko Macro.\n* **Key-Required / Gated Feeds:** NASA FIRMS Direct (`NASA_FIRMS_MAP_KEY`), AISHub (`AISHUB_USERNAME`).\n* **Broken / Forbidden Patterns:** Silent mock JSON fallback in `active_fire_dashboard` has been eliminated. When upstream APIs fail, the platform explicitly surfaces `SOURCE UNAVAILABLE`.\n\n---\n\n## F. Recommended Canonical Implementation for Each Layer\n\n1. **Map Engine:** High-performance Leaflet with hardware-accelerated tile layers (Tactical Dark, High-Res Esri Satellite, OpenTopoMap).\n2. **Orbital Mechanics Engine:** Self-contained, pure TypeScript analytical Keplerian + $J_2$ nodal precession SGP4 propagator running at 60 FPS.\n3. **Data Provenance System:** Every observation entity retains:\n   - `provider`\n   - `sourceUrl`\n   - `adapter`\n   - `fetched_at` timestamp\n   - `freshness_seconds` latency\n   - `status` (`VERIFIED LIVE`, `STATIC DATA`, `REQUIRES KEY`, `SOURCE UNAVAILABLE`)\n   - `raw_identifier`\n\n---\n\n## G. Proposed GOD-VIEW-LAB Architecture\n\n```\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\2