      text: "Make it without any api keys , fix the errors \n\nYes. This is the target I would lock in for God View. I checked the live Argos Atlas map, its current screenshots, methodology, Mumbai implementation, and infrastructure pages. Visually and architecturally, this is much closer to what ASTRA should become than the God\342\200\231s Eye implementation we were previously chasing. \n\nThe key point is: copy the interaction model and design language, not Argos\342\200\231s proprietary application/code.\n\nWhat I want ASTRA God View to match\n\nThe Argos design has a very good information hierarchy:\n\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202 ARGOS / SEARCH              LIVE STATS / STATUS      \342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\254\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244\n\342\224\202               \342\224\202                           \342\224\202          \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Detail Card   \342\224\202                           \342\224\202 Layers   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202               \342\224\202         MAP               \342\224\202 Filters  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Camera        \342\224\202                           \342\224\202          \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Company       \342\224\202      \342\227\211 \342\227\211  \342\234\210  \342\232\223  \342\232\241       \342\224\202 Cameras  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Flight        \342\224\202                           \342\224\202 Flights  \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Ship          \342\224\202                           \342\224\202 Ships    \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Power Plant   \342\224\202                           \342\224\202 Power    \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 News/Event    \342\224\202                           \342\224\202 News     \342\224\202\n\342\224\202               \342\224\202                           \342\224\202 Weather  \342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244\n\342\224\202 coordinates / source / freshness / map controls     \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n\nThat is what we should reproduce.\n\nNot five separate pages called Cameras / Flights / Ships / Power / News.\n\nOne map. Everything becomes a layer.\n\nArgos itself describes exactly that idea: cameras, flights, vessels, airports, ports, power plants and other infrastructure all appear on one interactive map. \n\nThe design details worth copying\n\nThe best parts are surprisingly mundane, which is usually the sign that the design is actually good:\n\n* very dark almost-black basemap\n* thin grey road/network lines\n* restrained neon cyan/green/amber status colours\n* tiny Bloomberg-terminal-style typography\n* floating translucent panels rather than huge cards\n* icon-based layer selector\n* contextual left/detail card\n* object selection without leaving the map\n* dense information without giant buttons\n* visual clustering at lower zoom\n* richer individual objects as you zoom\n* universal search\n* live/system status indicators\n* source/freshness information attached to observations\n* satellite/dark/terrain basemap switching\n\nThe official screenshots also show exactly the kind of side-panel + live-map combination you were describing earlier. \n\nAnd the #power=63031 URL is particularly interesting\n\nThat is the behaviour I want.\n\nInstead of just:\n\n/god-view\n\nwe want addressable objects:\n\n/god-view#power=<id>\n/god-view#company=<id>\n/god-view#port=<id>\n/god-view#flight=<id>\n/god-view#ship=<id>\n/god-view#camera=<id>\n\nSo someone could send a link to a specific refinery, port or power station and ASTRA opens directly on that object with its intelligence card open.\n\nThat is a small feature technically, but a massive UX improvement.\n\n\342\270\273\n\nHow I\342\200\231d make yours BETTER for finance\n\nWe should not make a generic Argos clone.\n\nMake:\n\nASTRA WORLD\n\nSame UI philosophy, but investment-first.\n\nFor example, clicking a power plant shouldn\342\200\231t stop at:\n\nTrombay Thermal Power Station\nFuel: Coal/Oil\nCapacity: xxx MW\n\nASTRA could eventually show:\n\nTROMBAY POWER\n\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\nOperator       Tata Power\nSector         Utilities\nCapacity       \342\200\246\nFuel           \342\200\246\nStatus         Operating\nMARKET\nTATAPOWER      \342\202\271xxx.xx\n1D             +x.xx%\n30D            +x.xx%\nASTRA\nTechnical      HOLD\nTrend          Bullish\nRisk           Medium\nPHYSICAL CONTEXT\nNearby ports           3\nShips nearby           47\nWeather alerts         0\nRelevant news          6\nGrid assets nearby     \342\200\246\nSOURCE\nDataset \342\200\246\nUpdated \342\200\246\n\nThen:\n\nOpen Company \342\206\222 ASTRA\n\nOpen Fundamentals \342\206\222 FMB\n\nOpen Technicals \342\206\222 TECHNICALS\n\nNow God View isn\342\200\231t a gimmick. It becomes another interface into the systems you\342\200\231ve already built.\n\n\342\270\273\n\nCameras can work exactly like Argos\n\nTheir methodology confirms that camera images come from public traffic/mobility authority portals, the source is credited, they retain only the latest frame, and they don\342\200\231t perform face or licence-plate recognition. \n\nTheir current published scale is about 177,700 public cameras/webcams, with roughly 16,900 live-video streams and the remainder mainly refreshing images. \n\nClick:\n\n\360\237\223\267 Camera\n\nand get something like:\n\n\342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n\342\224\202 CAM \302\267 MH-XXXX            \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 \342\227\217 LIVE                   \342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244\n\342\224\202                          \342\224\202\n\342\224\202       CAMERA IMAGE       \342\224\202\n\342\224\202                          \342\224\202\n\342\224\234\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\244\n\342\224\202 Provider: Official DOT   \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Updated: 12 sec ago      \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Type: Snapshot           \342\224\202\n\342\224\202 Source: \342\206\227                \342\224\202\n\342\224\224\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\230\n\nNo fake feed = no camera.\n\nIf the endpoint dies:\n\nSOURCE OFFLINE\nLast verified: 19:37 IST\n\nNot some cached stock image quietly pretending Mumbai traffic has looked identical for three weeks.\n\n\342\270\273\n\nOne reality check about India\n\nThis is important.\n\nArgos\342\200\231s own Mumbai page, published September 15, 2026, says Mumbai currently has only two public camera feeds in its dataset, both refreshing still images. It explicitly says it does not have public street-camera feeds for the Sea Link, Western Express Highway, Eastern Freeway, etc. \n\nSo:\n\nGlobal public-camera layer: absolutely.\n\n177k genuinely accessible Indian cameras: no.\n\nWe should fail closed where feeds aren\342\200\231t public instead of making Google AI Studio invent them.\n\n\342\270\273\n\nThe basemap is reproducible too\n\nArgos officially attributes:\n\nCARTO for base-map tiles, OpenStreetMap for map data, and Esri/Maxar/Earthstar for satellite imagery. \n\nI cannot verify from their public documentation whether their frontend renderer itself is MapLibre, Leaflet, Cesium or something custom, so I would not claim we know their exact frontend stack.\n\nWe don\342\200\231t need to.\n\nFor ASTRA I\342\200\231d use approximately:\n\nReact + TypeScript\n        \342\224\202\n    MapLibre GL\n        \342\224\202\n  \342\224\214\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\264\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\200\342\224\220\n deck.gl     CARTO/OSM\n  \342\224\202\nlarge live\ndatasets\nOptional:\nCesiumJS \342\206\222 3D globe / terrain / satellite mode\n\nAnd importantly:\n\nDO NOT LOAD 177,000 OBJECTS INTO REACT.\n\nInstead:\n\nworld\n \342\206\223\nclusters\n \342\206\223\ncountry\n \342\206\223\nregional objects\n \342\206\223\ncity\n \342\206\223\nindividual assets\n \342\206\223\nclick\n \342\206\223\nfull detail\n\nViewport-based querying + clustering + WebGL.\n\nThat is how you get the Argos feeling without your MacBook becoming an emergency heating appliance.\n\n\342\270\273\n\nWhat I would change in our current plan\n\nBefore seeing this specific Argos implementation, I was comfortable letting AI Studio synthesize ideas from all the ZIPs.\n\nI\342\200\231ve changed my recommendation slightly.\n\nMake Argos Atlas the UI/UX specification.\n\nUse the ZIP repositories as implementation donors.\n\nSo:\n\nARGOS ATLAS\n      \342\206\223\nDESIGN / UX TARGET\nGod\'s Eye\nWorldMonitor\nProvenance\nOpen Live Map\nGigawatt Map\nTerriaJS\ncamera repos\n      \342\206\223\nCODE + DATA-SOURCE REFERENCES\n      \342\206\223\nGOOGLE AI STUDIO\nGOD-VIEW-LAB\n      \342\206\223\nCLAUDE AUDIT\n      \342\206\223\nASTRA GOD VIEW\n\nDo not tell AI Studio:\n\ncombine these projects and make something cool.\n\nTell it:\n\nReproduce the interaction architecture and visual density of this Argos Atlas reference while implementing the functionality using the supplied open-source repositories and verified public data sources.\n\nHuge difference.\n\n\342\270\273\n\nAnd I would make Argos the visual benchmark\n\nFor the prototype:\n\nVisual fidelity target: ~90%+ of the overall interaction/design feel.\n\nFunctional target: every visible live layer must actually work or explicitly say unavailable.\n\nData target: 100% provenance.\n\nFake-data tolerance: zero.\n\nThen add ASTRA-exclusive layers:\n\nCOMPANIES\nNSE/BSE stocks\nASSETS\nplants\nfactories\nmines\nrefineries\nwarehouses\nports\nMARKETS\nindices\ncommodities\nFX\nINTELLIGENCE\nnews\nweather\nnatural events\nsupply chain\ntrade flows\nASTRA\nsignals\ntechnicals\nrisk\nFMB\nfundamentals\nvaluation\nsector metrics\n\nThat is now the design direction I would lock.\n\nArgos UI/UX + WorldMonitor intelligence + God\342\200\231s Eye/live-map capabilities + Provenance camera architecture + Gigawatt physical infrastructure + your ASTRA/FMB/TECHNICALS financial layer.\n\nThat is materially stronger than our previous generic \342\200\234God View\342\200\235 concept.Yes. For the second batch, I\342\200\231d add these. The first three matter specifically for the live public-camera layer.\n\n1. Provenance \342\200\224 this is the best extra one I found. It has 41 live layers and, importantly, 11 keyless government road-camera networks including TfL, Caltrans, SCDOT, Finland Digitraffic, Oregon TripCheck, DriveBC, NZTA, Iceland, Estonia and Traffic Scotland. It also proxies camera media through an allow-listed backend rather than accepting arbitrary URLs. That architecture is exactly what I\342\200\231d want AI Studio to study. \n    Download/source: 011-sam-110/Provenance\342\201\240\357\277\274\n2. Argus Global Camera Intelligence \342\200\224 dedicated camera implementation with 200k+ public traffic/webcam entries, React/TypeScript frontend plus Python ingestion pipeline. Useful for learning large-scale camera indexing and clustering. \n    Download/source: GoSlowPoke168/Argus\342\201\240\357\277\274\n3. OpenTrafficCamMap \342\200\224 much simpler camera dataset/architecture, around 7,500 traffic cameras, organized geographically. Good as a clean fallback/reference rather than another giant application. \n    Download/source: AidanWelch/OpenTrafficCamMap\342\201\240\357\277\274\n\nThen add these rendering/analytics donors if you really want to give AI Studio the full toolbox:\n\n4. MapLibre GL JS \342\200\224 primary open-source WebGL map renderer. BSD-3-Clause. \n    Download/source: maplibre/maplibre-gl-js\342\201\240\357\277\274\n5. deck.gl \342\200\224 GPU rendering for very large point sets, routes, arcs, heat maps and clusters. MIT. Very relevant when the UI has thousands of cameras/events. \n    Download/source: visgl/deck.gl\342\201\240\357\277\274\n6. Kepler.gl \342\200\224 geospatial analytics UI, filtering, layer controls and time-based exploration. MIT. \n    Download/source: keplergl/kepler.gl\342\201\240\357\277\274\n7. CesiumJS \342\200\224 serious 3D globe/terrain engine. Apache-2.0. \n    Download/source: CesiumGS/cesium\342\201\240\357\277\274\n\nSo your total upload set becomes\n\nFIRST BATCH\n1 Gods Eye View\n2 WorldMonitor\n3 Open Live Map\n4 Gigawatt Map\n5 Active Fire Dashboard\n6 TerriaJS\nSECOND BATCH\n7 Provenance                  \342\206\220 VERY IMPORTANT\n8 Argus                      \342\206\220 LIVE CAMERA FOCUS\n9 OpenTrafficCamMap          \342\206\220 CAMERA DATA/REFERENCE\n10 MapLibre GL JS\n11 deck.gl\n12 Kepler.gl\n13 CesiumJS\n\nFor live cameras, tell AI Studio to use only public-by-design feeds, especially government transport, weather, tourism and infrastructure cameras. No private CCTV discovery, no scanning for exposed home/business cameras, no facial recognition, no licence-plate recognition, and no tracking people between feeds.\n\nAlso, don\342\200\231t let it interpret camera URL exists as camera verified live. Require:\n\nCAMERA\n\342\206\222 provider\n\342\206\222 official/public source\n\342\206\222 coordinates\n\342\206\222 media type (snapshot/HLS/etc.)\n\342\206\222 HTTP/live test\n\342\206\222 last_verified_at\n\342\206\222 freshness\n\342\206\222 attribution\n\342\206\222 LIVE / STALE / OFFLINE\n\nThat last requirement matters enormously. Otherwise AI Studio will happily put 200,000 pins on Earth while 130,000 of them lead to the digital equivalent of a boarded-up Blockbuster.\n\nMost valuable new ZIP: Provenance. Its camera implementation is considerably closer to what we actually want for ASTRA because the repo explicitly documents official government camera networks, normalized adapters, attribution, coverage limitations and server-side media proxying."
    }
  }
}
